      "upstream_fields": {
        "description": "description: \"Reviews diffs, PRs, release readiness, and publishing follow-through. Use when asked to review, triage issues or PRs, or ship. Not for debugging root causes or prose.\"\n",
        "when_to_use": "when_to_use: \"review, 看看代码, 检查一下, 合并前, 看看issue, 看看PR, release, publish, push, 发布, 提交, close issue, 关闭issue, release reaction, 发布表情, before merge, 值得发布, code review, code-review, audit, 项目体检, 项目评分, scorecard\"\n",
        "dispatch_intent": "dispatch_intent: \"Code review, before merge, release gates, generated artifacts, safety sinks, publish/push/reaction follow-through, triage issues/PRs, project-wide code-quality audit scorecard\"\n"
      },
      "reason": [
        "Preserve the full upstream description and dispatch_intent verbatim, and retain every original when_to_use phrase, order and separator. Insert separately identified local trigger items at existing list boundaries only; keep Chinese display text in metadata.zh_description. For fields absent upstream, retain the explicitly local values. Preserve local license/version and frozen policy.",
        "Keep the required host salutation and output format instead of the upstream marker.",
        "Preserve standing necessary repair authorization without broadening external writes.",
        "Do not require redundant per-finding approval when repair is already authorized.",
        "Retain local risk-based depth; line and file counts cannot choose review severity.",
        "Keep repair classification aligned with existing authorization.",
        "Respect existing authorization in autofix routing.",
        "Keep the existing OCR adapter, complete task scope and proportional verification alongside the restored upstream review modes.",
        "Document the discovery default and explicit execution path."
      ],
